The database is torn down after each test, so every test starts with zero rows. """ ...

# tests/conftest.py import pytest from fastapi.testclient import TestClient
@pytest.fixture def client(db_session) -> TestClient: """A TestClient for app.main:app with get_db overridden to yield `db_session`.
The override is what makes a request issued through this client and a query issued through the `db_session` fixture see the SAME rows - which is what the "store nothing" assertions in tests 4 and 5 below depend on. The real database file is never touched. """ ...

